### Pigeon - Communication API scenarios (IntelliJ HTTP client or VS Code REST Client)
### Start the app with the local profile first. Change the Idempotency-Key values to re-run.

@base = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Accept a payment receipt -> 202 QUEUED
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-receipt-001
X-Correlation-Id: demo-corr-001

{
  "templateId": "payment-receipt",
  "recipient": "dana@example.com",
  "stream": "TRANSACTIONAL",
  "variables": {
    "firstName": "Dana",
    "amount": "$412.60",
    "paidOn": "November 6, 2026",
    "last4": "4417"
  }
}

### 2. Same key, same body -> 202, same requestId, Idempotent-Replayed: true
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-receipt-001

{
  "templateId": "payment-receipt",
  "recipient": "DANA@example.com",
  "stream": "TRANSACTIONAL",
  "variables": { "last4": "4417", "paidOn": "November 6, 2026", "amount": "$412.60", "firstName": "Dana" }
}

### 3. Same key, different body -> 422 idempotency-key-reused
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-receipt-001

{
  "templateId": "payment-receipt",
  "recipient": "someone.else@example.com",
  "stream": "TRANSACTIONAL",
  "variables": { "firstName": "Sam", "amount": "$10.00", "paidOn": "November 6, 2026", "last4": "0001" }
}

### 4. Enrollment confirmation as XML -> 202 (template version 2)
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/xml
Accept: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-enroll-001

<communication>
  <templateId>enrollment-confirmation</templateId>
  <recipient>dana@example.com</recipient>
  <stream>TRANSACTIONAL</stream>
  <variables>
    <firstName>Dana</firstName>
    <planName>Gold PPO 2027</planName>
    <effectiveDate>January 1, 2027</effectiveDate>
    <memberId>AB-448210</memberId>
  </variables>
</communication>

### 5. Bulk stream -> configuration set pigeon-bulk-prod
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-bulk-001

{
  "templateId": "payment-receipt",
  "recipient": "dana@example.com",
  "stream": "BULK",
  "variables": { "firstName": "Dana", "amount": "$412.60", "paidOn": "November 6, 2026", "last4": "4417" }
}

### 6. Missing merge fields -> 400 with missingFields
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-missing-001

{
  "templateId": "payment-receipt",
  "recipient": "dana@example.com",
  "stream": "TRANSACTIONAL",
  "variables": { "firstName": "Dana" }
}

### 7. Invalid fields -> 400 listing every field error
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-invalid-001

{ "templateId": "", "recipient": "not-an-email", "variables": {} }

### 8. Unknown template -> 400 unknown-template
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-unknown-001

{ "templateId": "no-such-template", "recipient": "dana@example.com", "stream": "TRANSACTIONAL", "variables": {} }

### 9. Missing Idempotency-Key -> 400
POST {{base}}/v1/communications
Content-Type: application/json

{ "templateId": "payment-receipt", "recipient": "dana@example.com", "stream": "TRANSACTIONAL", "variables": {} }

### 10. Status and history (paste a requestId from request 1)
GET {{base}}/v1/communications/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/json

### 11. Health
GET {{base}}/actuator/health
